; A Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, C#, PHP, C++ or Kotlin catch body, a Python
; except body, or a Ruby rescue body is structurally empty, including
; comment-only bodies and Python pass/ellipsis.
; Recovered or unavailable syntax remains unknown. This does not claim that
; the handler is reachable or that its exception type can be thrown.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.correctness.empty-failure-handler"
  :name "Empty failure handler"
  :message "this failure handler contains no failure-handling statements"
  :severity warning
  :description "An exact Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, C#, PHP, C++ or Kotlin catch clause, Python except clause, or Ruby rescue clause has no body statements other than comments, empty statements, or Python pass and ellipsis. A C# exception filter selects an exception but does not handle it. Promise rejection callbacks, the Ruby rescue modifier and Scala catch cases are not covered. This is a structural review finding: it does not establish that the handler is reachable or that its exception type can be thrown. Recovered or unavailable syntax is inconclusive. Review whether the exception needs handling or propagation; comments do not count as handling. No automatic fix is supplied."
  :help-uri "https://bifrost.brokk.ai/static-analysis-policies/#built-in-code-smell-pack"
  :tags ["correctness" "exceptions"]
  :analysis (analysis
    :type assertion
    (bind :name handler
      :query (rql :schema-version 1
        (filter :where ((verdict eq empty)
                        (proof eq exact)
                        (coverage eq exhaustive))
          (failure-handler-state
            (language java javascript typescript python csharp php cpp kotlin ruby (catch))))))
    (group :name by-handler :by (handler.id)
      (aggregate :name empty-handlers :op count))
    (assert :group by-handler :value empty-handlers :cardinality (exactly 0))))
